    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d61-a1">

                <pb facs="0120" n="774" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg774"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 151.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terashima to Mr.
                            Bingham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokei</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="japanese-nengō"
                            when="1874-11-10"><hi rendition="#italic">the 10th, 11th month, the 7th
                                year of Meiji</hi></date>. (November 10, 1874.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 94.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: The shooting regulations, as
                    per inclosure A, and the penaregulations for violation thereof by foreigners,
                    inclosure B, having been framed, the undersigned begs to submit them to your
                    excellency, and will feel obliged to have your reply, whether they meet with
                    your approval or not.</p>
                <p>With great respect,</p>
                <closer><signed>TERASHIMA MUNENORI,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">H. I. J. M’s.
                            Minister for F. A.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">John A. Bingham</hi>, &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
